  "limits": "Single-column forward/inverse FFT with cached powers and end normalization in both methods; candidate splits each stage into two disjoint tasks using the supplied two-worker strategy, including the final single-block stage; bit reversal and normalization remain serial. The explicit screen pool preparation is separate, and transforms never create a pool on an actual validated Transfer opening polynomial; no keys or proof generation. Preparation and eight-MiB tables plus one inverse-size scalar are separate. Three warmups and five samples per method/operation, alternating order; each clock includes allocation/copy/transform, with equality checks and output cleanup outside. Existing multi-column NTT and verifier paths are untouched. No full-API speedup or phone claim."
